         Agendas & Minutes Agendas are available before the meetings. Minutes are available and approved. View Most Recent Agendas and Minutes Staff Kathleen K. Farrell, Town Clerk, Notary Public Phone 978-422-8111, ext. 2308 Shane Rhodes, Assistant Town Clerk, Notary Public Phone 978-422-8111, ext. 2307 Overview Mission One of the oldest government positions in New England, the Town Clerk is the gateway to the Town and a resource of information. We are the keepers of the records, documenting the history of Sterling. This office has records and letters from the early 1700s. All permanent records are currently stored in the Town's vault. These records include birth, marriage, and death records, Town Reports, Selectmen's minutes, Street Lists, census, business certificates, dog licenses, fuel tank licenses, and a myriad of legal documents and maps. The Town Clerk is mandated by the Secretary of State, Attorney General's Office, and the Department of Revenue (DLS Division) to maintain compliance with approximately 376 Massachusetts General Laws. 
     

 
